: "synth/r1/zngr", "date": ""}}, {"id": "03f9c4dfb613", "entryId": "zngr", "kind": "question", "stage": "synthesis", "target": {}, "summary": "Can a native speaker provide a literal metal-rusting context for comparison? The supplied textual example supports only figurative hands rusting through disuse.", "before": null, "after": null, "data": {}, "rationale": "", "evidence": [], "priority": 2, "provenance": {"model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "effort": "xhigh", "protocol": "SYNTH_PROTOCOL", "run": "synth/r1/zngr", "date": ""}}, {"id": "a0ec706255c5", "entryId": "zngr", "kind": "fix-text", "stage": "proofreading", "target": {"stemId": "zngr.I", "boxId": "zngr.I.d.infectum", "exampleId": "zngr.I.d.infectum.1", "field": "translation"}, "summary": "Correct rostetet to rostet", "before": "rostetet", "after": "rostet", "data": {"confidence": "high"}, "rationale": "rostetet is an erroneous verb ending here. The quoted k-mizangər is singular Infectum and the gloss is einrosten, giving rostet ein.", "evidence": [], "priority": 3, "provenance": {"model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "effort": "high", "protocol": "PROOF_PROTOCOL", "run": "proof/P071", "date": "2026-10-25"}}, {"id": "28d6e2d57641", "entryId": "zngr", "kind": "note", "stage": "synthesis", "target": {"stemId": "zngr.I", "sense": "1"}, "summary": "Hands are figuratively rusted through inactivity; the following me zawno lo šaġənno explicitly links the state to not having worked. This is the only contextual rust example supplied.", "before": null, "after": null, "data": {"type": "extension"}, "rationale": "", "evidence": [{"textId": "R073", "v": 429, "cite": "73/429"}], "priority": 3, "provenance": {"model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "effort": "xhigh", "protocol": "SYNTH_PROTOCOL", "run": "synth/r1/zngr", "date": ""}}]